               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Notes from the Field: Opioid-Involved Overdose Deaths with Fentanyl or Fentanyl Analogs Detected â€” 28 States and the District of Columbia, July 2016â€“December 2018</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:title>
         <dc:description>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The declines in overdose deaths with fentanyl analogs (carfentanil, furanylfentanyl, acrylfentanyl, and cyclopropylfentanyl) detected contributed to declines in opioid-involved overdose deaths during 2018 among a subset of states, even as deaths with fentanyl detected increased over time, which highlights the continued need to test for fentanyl analogs.</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:description>
         <dc:creator>
            <rdf:Bag/>
         </dc:creator>
